fastmcp (4.0.0~a2-1.1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Pragmatic dependency adjustment: Use flexible version constraints
    for python3-mcp to work with existing Debian repo state
  * Remove python3-httpx2 and python3-mcp-types hard dependencies
    (designed for future repo state with updated packages)
  * Effective for internal deployments where fastmcp 4.0.0a2 is
    installed via pip alongside the package

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Fri, 25 Jul 2026 11:15:00 +0200

fastmcp (4.0.0~a2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Update to upstream v4.0.0a2
  * NEW: fastmcp_remote and fastmcp_tasks workspace members added
  * FIXED: Remove websockets-sansio dependency (no longer used in v4.0.0)
  * Update dependencies: mcp-types==2.0.0b2, authlib>=1.2.0, cyclopts>=0.13.0
  * Workspace restructure: now includes fastmcp_slim (core), fastmcp_remote
    (remote protocol), and fastmcp_tasks (task execution)

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Fri, 25 Jul 2026 11:00:00 +0200

fastmcp (3.4.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Update to upstream v3.4.2
  * Upstream split fastmcp into a thin "fastmcp" meta-package plus the
    real implementation in the fastmcp_slim/ workspace member; build
    python3-fastmcp from fastmcp_slim/ instead of the repository root
  * Add debian/patch-pyproject.py to statically pin version and flatten
    fastmcp_slim's base + mcp + client + server extras into one
    dependency list, replacing the previous root pyproject.toml sed patch
  * Add python3-pydantic-settings, python3-typing-extensions,
    python3-starlette, python3-joserfc, python3-python-multipart
    dependencies pulled in by the new upstream dependency set

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Tue, 30 Jun 2026 22:57:24 +0200

